{
 "id": "206-14",
 "split": "screen_long",
 "sentences": [
  "Mentoring is a two-way street, so please feel free to reach out if there's anything you need or any questions you have along the way.",
  "That's why I want you to never use a pre-commit hook.",
  "Pre-commit hooks can sometimes cause issues and conflicts, especially in a large codebase like ours.",
  "Instead, we rely on our continuous integration (CI) system to catch any issues before changes are merged into the main branch.",
  "Our CI system is set up to automatically run a suite of tests and static code analysis tools whenever a pull request is opened.",
  "This way, you'll get feedback on any issues or violations of our coding standards, and you can address them before your code becomes a part of the main codebase.",
  "Absolutely.",
  "It's all about catching issues early and ensuring that only high-quality, well-tested code makes it into our main branch.",
  "I'll send you some documentation and resources on our CI system and the specific tests and checks we use.",
  "Now, I want to discuss a coding convention I'd like you to follow from now on.",
  "It's important for consistency and readability.",
  "Consistency is key, and it will really help the team when we're reviewing and collaborating on code.",
  "Keep up the good work, and don't hesitate to reach out if you have any questions or concerns.",
  "I know we've discussed this before, but I want to emphasize the importance of using a pre-commit hook from now on.",
  "It's a crucial step to ensure code quality and consistency.",
  "A pre-commit hook is basically a script that runs automatically before any code is committed to the repository.",
  "But in essence, you'll need to install a pre-commit package for Python."
 ],
